+### CA Certificates from ClusterTrustBundles
+
+The `caCertificateRefs` of a `BackendTLSPolicy` and of the Gateway [frontend client certificate validation](#frontend-client-certificate-validation) can reference a [ClusterTrustBundle](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/certificate-signing-requests/#cluster-trust-bundles), as defined by [GEP-5075](https://gateway-api.sigs.k8s.io/geps/gep-5075/).
+A `ClusterTrustBundle` is cluster-scoped: the reference has no namespace and needs no `ReferenceGrant`.
+Traefik uses the PEM bundle in `spec.trustBundle` as the CA certificates.
+
+```yaml
+---
+apiVersion: gateway.networking.k8s.io/v1
+kind: BackendTLSPolicy
+metadata:
+  name: whoami-tls
+  namespace: default
+spec:
+  targetRefs:
+    - group: ""
+      kind: Service
+      name: whoami
+  validation:
+    caCertificateRefs:
+      - group: certificates.k8s.io
+        kind: ClusterTrustBundle
+        name: my-ca-bundle
+    hostname: whoami.example.com
+```
+
+Traefik watches `ClusterTrustBundle` resources only when both of these conditions are true at startup:
+
+| Condition | Otherwise, the `ResolvedRefs` condition message is |
+|-----------|----------------------------------------------------|
+| The cluster serves the `certificates.k8s.io/v1` API. | `ClusterTrustBundles are not supported, the cluster does not serve the certificates.k8s.io/v1 API` |
+| Traefik is allowed to `list` and `watch` `clustertrustbundles` in the `certificates.k8s.io` group, as in the [RBAC](../../dynamic-configuration/kubernetes-gateway-rbac.yml). | `ClusterTrustBundles are not supported, Traefik is not allowed to list and watch clustertrustbundles` |
+
+When the API or the permissions are added later, restart Traefik to use `ClusterTrustBundle` references.
